  "story": [
    "<p>After a storm, a small farm needs one cleared lane from the barn door to the road. The yard is a grid of squares. The barn door is the top-left square and the gate to the road is the bottom-right one. Drifts are uneven, so each square takes a different number of minutes to plough.</p>",
    "<p>The plough only drives forward, so the lane can only go <strong>right</strong> or <strong>down</strong> from square to square. Which lane takes the least time to clear?</p>"
  ],
  "task": [
    "<p>Write <code>minClearingTime(snow)</code>. <code>snow[r][c]</code> is the minutes needed to clear square <code>(r, c)</code>. Return the smallest total time of a lane that starts at the top-left square, ends at the bottom-right square, and moves one square right or down at each step.</p>",
    "<p>The total includes both the first and the last square. Return only the time, not the lane.</p>"
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ number of rows, number of columns ≤ 100",
    "Every row has the same length.",
    "0 ≤ snow[r][c] ≤ 100"
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
